--- body ---
## Context

Child of tickets/1004. The attribution record (spec §4) is the coaching
system's only capture: one journal entry per reviewed merge, fixed
grep-able lines, findings anchored repo-relative `path:line`, full model
ids pinned verbatim, attempt status recorded, writer line for
stratification.

## Actions

1. Define the record template (spec §4 shape) as the canonical example in
   the spec or a roar reference file; fixed field names, no prose in
   fact lines.
2. Extend roar step 6: when the merged PR was reviewed, write the
   attribution entry under the project's memory/journal/, including
   writer line (runtime, full model id, effort), one reviewer line per
   reviewer with attempt status (ran|failed|skipped), findings with
   repo-relative path:line anchors and adopted flags. No initial
   defect-confirmed placeholder: those are append-only event lines
   written by the 1006 hook.
3. Fail-loud capture: a reviewed PR whose record cannot name its
   reviewers is reported, never filled in from memory (spec §4.8).
4. Tests: template parses with a fixed-line reader; anchors are unique
   repo-relative path:line; full model id and status fields present;
   adopted findings parse as pre-merge defect labels.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Roar on a reviewed merge writes a valid attribution record
- [ ] A fixed-line reader (groundwork for 1007) parses it without prose
      heuristics

## Raid annotation (2026-10-03, imagine pass)
PREMISE: Holds. The record contract is approved on main (spec §4, PR #1114); the v8 gate is genuinely lifted (0909 closed No-rollout; 0913 lift 2026-10-03, PR #1160); the harness journal is live v8 (42 entries; write path pinned in `scripts/memory-capture.sh`, tested by `tests/test_memory_capture.sh`); step 6 already captures append-only journal entries through the same helper. No reader exists yet (`kind: review-attribution` appears only in docs — the spec example and two "convertible" samples in `docs/memory-v8/evaluation-results.md:253,276`). 0937 hand-off (log 10:24Z): the capture-side half is in scope and already covered by Actions 2–3 — a dead-auth seat becomes a named `reviewer: … status: failed` line plus fail-loud, which is a channel something other than a human reads; the active surface (a check over N runs) is the 1007 run-failure rate (spec §6) and is out of scope here.
REIMAGINE: Four touches + one log line. (a) Canonical template: spec §4 stays the single source; add one concretely valid capture instance (real values, verbatim provider-qualified model id, `kind: review-attribution` as line 1, no `defect-confirmed:` line) — never a verbatim copy of the existing illustration block (it carries a defect-confirmed line and placeholders). (b) Extend step 6 (`skills/roar/SKILL.md:152ff`, prose-only today): when a merged PR in the roar interval was reviewed (the session holds a review trail), write one `kind: review-attribution` entry per reviewed PR (slug `review-attribution-prNNNN`) through the same pinned helper and audience decision — writer line (runtime + full verbatim model id + effort), one reviewer line per reviewer with `status: ran|failed|skipped`, findings as repo-relative `path:line` + `adopted:`; no initial defect-confirmed line; fail-loud per §4.8 (a reviewed PR whose record cannot name its reviewers is reported in the step-11 summary, never filled in). No new fenced block (one-snippet-per-step precedent, `test_roar_step2_attribution.py`). (c) Fixed-line reader: new `scripts/attribution_record.py` (shared-substrate home per spec §3) — parse + validate + structured output; enforce vocabularies; anchors unique repo-relative path:line; accept defect-confirmed lines when present (1006 appends them); prose/context opaque; exit non-zero loudly on any violation. (d) Tests: `tests/test_attribution_record.py` — template parses verbatim; every required-line failure fails loud (kind, pr, writer, reviewer-without-status, missing model id); duplicate/non-repo-relative anchors rejected; prose-independence (two prose variants, identical fixed lines → identical parse); grep test that step 6 carries the reviewed-PR trigger and the fail-loud rule. (e) Log line disposing the 0937 hand-off (capture-side in, read-side → 1007).
ANTIPATTERNS: No prose parsing (fact lines carry no prose; the reader never reads context). No runtime-branded paths (project `memory/journal/` only; never `~/.claude`/`~/.pi`/`~/.codex`). No filling in from memory (§4.8 — no reconstructed model ids, no `model=unknown`; a seat that didn't run is a named `status: failed|skipped` line). No mutating existing journal entries (new record = new file via the helper, which refuses overwrite). No initial defect-confirmed placeholder (rule 5: zero lines when none yet) — while the reader must accept them. No overbuilding for 1007 (no catch rates, correlation, marginal coverage, board normalization, statistics). Do not touch step 2's celebration block (1009's teardown; capture lands before teardown, §10) and do not migrate `enumerate-merges.py` yet (step 2 still consumes it). Do not bypass `memory-capture.sh` (audience decision + overwrite refusal + path convention pinned there).
EXIT-CRITERIA: Box 1 — drivable seam: canonical template rendered with real values → `memory-capture.sh` → file at `memory/journal/YYYY/YYYY-MM-DD-review-attribution-prNNNN.md` → reader parses valid; plus the step-6 grep test. A full agent end-to-end ("which reviewers from the session trail") is not mechanically drivable — the step-2 snippet precedent defines the honest seam. Box 2 — `scripts/attribution_record.py` + tests as above. Verdict: keep-as-is (both boxes honest and drivable).

## Raid Imagine refresh (2026-10-05)
PREMISE: PASS; 0913 lift stands, harness capture helper is live, no implementation exists.
APPROACH: Concrete canonical template, roar reviewed-merge capture through existing audience-aware helper, standard-library fixed-line reader; fail loud on unavailable factual identities. Preserve 0937 capture-side disposition and defer statistics/teardown/backfill.
CORRECTION: Prior global anchor-uniqueness wording is superseded: identical anchors across reviewers are necessary shared-catch joins (spec section 4.4); reject duplicate findings within one reviewer and invalid repository-relative anchors. Follow current encrypted-in-repo capture policy, not superseded private-companion wording. Both exit criteria preserved.
VERIFICATION: Concrete template -> validation -> public capture helper -> parse resulting journal. Test prose independence, required facts, attempt statuses, cross-reviewer shared anchors and optional subsequent defect-confirmed events. Reviewed merges require capture even without a separate significant experience.
BLIND-SPOT: Multiple rounds may repeat reviewers/statuses; real PR 1164 round-3 trail confirms distinct regression and failed-seat attempts. Preserve reviewer lines as attempts rather than collapsing by model/seat; factual attempt-qualified seat roles fit existing name-or-role field. Source round/revision belongs in opaque context; no schema additions or guessed identities. Shared anchors remain join keys; unavailable historical evidence fails loud.

## Raid Plan (2026-10-05)
Actions: Concrete template in spec; reusable fixed-line parse/validate/JSON reader and small validation-before-capture mode reusing memory-capture.sh; roar step-6 reviewed-merge capture and visible failure; tests for facts, statuses, shared anchors, optional later defect events and prose independence.
First test: In temporary Git project, capture valid record with shared adopted anchor across two reviewers and a failed third attempt; parse actual journal bytes and verify identities/status/labels. Missing status must fail before writing. Use child_env and integration markers. Paths: spec, roar, script, tests, ticket (5). 1006/1007 consume parser but are not dependencies; no stats, teardown or helper-policy changes.

## Raid feasibility (2026-10-05)
PASS: Existing paths/signatures verified; 5 content paths per ticket below review breaker; no credentials for public capture fixtures, no new package, no shared implementation path/registry, no coordination PR. Behavioral fixtures must count log entries only and retain legacy categories; capture round-trip must preserve cross-reviewer shared anchors and separate attempts.
